From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:42:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] test(chem108): browser coverage for late account answers,
 account switch, cross-tab sign-out and restore

The trial page runs with the real js/mcc-auth.js and the real bar. Only
the account service's HTTP replies are a fixture, held per bearer token
until released, so a "late" answer is a reply that really arrives late:

- sign-out while the lookup is out, then the answer arrives
- another tab signs in as a second account; the first account's answer
  arrives first, then the second's
- a verified member mid-round: another tab refreshes the same member's
  token (the round goes on), then signs out (the round closes)
- account service unreachable with trial days left: the preview stays
- a real back/forward-cache restore after signing out on the page the
  member went to, in a browser launched with that cache on; printed as
  NOT RUN when the build reloads instead of restoring

On the previous trial module the first, second, third and fifth cases
fail; the fourth is the control.

